Difference

set token in cookie, has XSS risks, only used by browser, front-end do not intervent
handle token by front-end, store in localStorage, can be used on other devices for auth, and not only on browser

use the old way, set cookie by server to save token, it can download some files without front-end but still auth with token

When the browser makes a request to the server (e.g., to download a file), it automatically includes the cookie in the request headers for the same domain, as long as the cookie’s Path and SameSite attributes allow it.

the new way is token as parameter to post or get for auth in request

